meta {
  name: Create User
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/create
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "discordAccount": {
      "discordId": 222222222,
      "username": "ExampleDiscordUser"
    },
    "runescapeAccounts": []
  }
}

docs {
  Returns temporary login credentials for the new user (see
  ICredentialStore.CreateTemporaryCredentialsAsync) -- copy them from the
  response if you want to log in as this user separately.

  The new user's id equals discordId (UserCreatedEvent sets UserId =
  discordAccount.DiscordId), which is why Promote/Demote User default their
  target to 222222222 -- run this request first and those two work as-is.

  Real Discord snowflakes exceed 2^53 and can lose precision if entered
  through a UI that round-trips the body via JS numbers (e.g. Bruno's visual
  JSON editor). Edit this body in raw/code mode instead of the tree view to
  keep the literal digits intact -- the Api has no JsonNumberHandling
  configured, so a quoted string here would fail to deserialize.
}
